Table 7 :

planning_solution.replenishment.sto_table

Description : Stock Transfer Order (STO) header/lines - the PRIMARY transfer table. One STO can have many lines
(one per article). Trace the full journey source -> destination via sto_number across obd_table (outbound)
and ibd_table (inbound).

sto_number - the STO id (join key to obd_table / ibd_table)
created_date - STO create date, STRING format YYYYMMDD (e.g. '20260806')
transfer_type - SAP transfer type code (ZICT / ZIAP = store-to-store; ZICR/ZTLT/ZCCR/ZIPT = DC->store replenishment; etc.)
source_location - sending site (PLANT)   |   destination_location - receiving site (PLANT)
article - variant article   |   sto_qty - qty requested on the line
obd_status / ibd_status - roll-up status of the outbound / inbound leg (Completed / ...)

STORE-TO-STORE TRANSFERS = source_location AND destination_location are BOTH PLANTCAT='A' stores
(join both to Table 2 store master). Both PLANTCAT='B' or B->A = warehouse/DC replenishment (exclude for
store-to-store). No cost column - approximate value via atp_detail.unit_cost_aed joined on article.


Table 8 :

planning_solution.replenishment.obd_table

Description : OUTBOUND delivery details for an STO (pick / pack / PGI = dispatch). Join to Table 7 on sto_number (+ sto_line_number).

obd_number - outbound delivery id   |   obd_created_date (DATE)   |   obd_qty   |   obd_status ('C' = completed)
pick_pack_plan_timestamp / pick_pack_completion_timestamp / pgi_timestamp - PGI = Post Goods Issue = stock dispatched from source


Table 9 :

planning_solution.replenishment.ibd_table

Description : INBOUND delivery details for an STO (goods receipt at destination). Join to Table 7 on sto_number (+ sto_line_number).

ibd_number - inbound delivery id   |   ibd_created_date (DATE)   |   ibd_qty   |   ibd_status
grn_qty - qty actually received (GRN)   |   grn_timestamp - Goods Receipt time at destination (transfer complete)

